NOTICE — aa-intelligence-index-reverse
======================================

Last updated: 2026-09-29

0. Methodology change v4.1.1 -> v4.3.2
----------------------------------------
On 2026-09-29 the AA methodology page versions the Index as v4.3.2:
10 evaluations / 11 score components, categories Agents 30 / Coding 20 /
Scientific Reasoning 20 / General 30. This repo tracks the change as:
new files data/weights_v4.3.2.csv, data/models_v4.3.2.csv and
calculator default v4.3.2; the v4.1.1 files (data/weights_v4.1.1.csv,
data/models.csv, examples/claude-opus-5.json, examples/kimi-k3.json)
are frozen archives. No v4.3.2 public component dump is in the repo yet;
the first full 11-component dump is the top contribution (see
CONTRIBUTING.md). The GDP.pdf choice (All-pass headline as s) is
documented as an open point in docs/methodology.md §0.

1. What this project is
-----------------------
An independent, community reconstruction of the scoring formula behind the
**Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index** (methodology v4.1.1), shipped as:

- a machine-readable weights table (`data/weights_v4.3.2.csv`, current;
  `data/weights_v4.1.1.csv`, archive)
- machine-readable matrices of public component scores
  (`data/models_v4.3.2.csv`, pending first dump; `data/models.csv`, 8-model v4.1.1 archive)
- a small, dependency-free calculator (`src/aa_index.py`)
- a worked example reproducing the published v4.1.1 Index of 8 models to within
  |Delta| <= 0.30 (see `examples/` and the README)

