3. Data provenance
------------------
- The weights come from the public methodology pages of Artificial
  Analysis (v4.3.2 current, v4.1.1 archived 2026-09-01/02):
  https://artificialanalysis.ai/methodology/intelligence-benchmarking
  https://artificialanalysis.ai/evaluations/artificial-analysis-intelligence-index
  https://artificialanalysis.ai/articles/artificial-analysis-intelligence-index-v4-1
- The v4.3.2 component scores (29 rows in `data/models_v4.3.2.csv`) were read
  from the public Index-page data payload on artificialanalysis.ai on
  2026-09-29 (page URL in every row's `source`). No private data, no scraped
  paywalled content, no redistribution of raw HTML.
- The "Index AA" column in `data/models.csv` is the value publicly
  displayed by Artificial Analysis for each model at the same date.

4. What you may do
------------------
- Reuse the formula, the code and the data files with attribution
  (MIT for code; the weights themselves are CC BY 4.0 via Artificial
  Analysis — attribute Artificial Analysis when redistributing them).
- Submit PRs to add models: each new row MUST include the source URL and
  the date of the AA chart dump (see CONTRIBUTING.md).

5. Known limits (do not oversell the result)
--------------------------------------------
- The v4.3.2 reconstruction is validated on 29 live models, Index ~14-58
  (max |Delta| 0.12, 2026-09-29). The v4.1.1 archive was validated ONLY on
  the band ~56-63 (8 models, max |Delta| 0.30).
- All deltas are <= 0, consistent with rounding noise in the public
  component scores, not with a structural formula error.
- The Elo <-> model-variant mapping (e.g. "Grok 4.6 (high)") was done by
  hand; a wrong row would fail loudly in recomputation, the other rows
  would not be affected.
